NAME
       ballerina-init - Initialize the dependencies of a Ballerina package

SYNOPSIS
       bal init


DESCRIPTION
       Initialize the dependencies of the Ballerina package in the current
       directory, or of the package that contains it. In a workspace, the
       packages it depends on in the workspace are initialized too. At the root
       of a workspace, all its packages are initialized.

       Each dependency is resolved to the latest version with the same major
       version as the one given in 'Ballerina.toml'.

       Pulls the dependencies that are not available locally, compiles them
       into the dependency cache, and writes the resolved versions to
       'Dependencies.toml'. Later builds use the compiled dependencies from the
       cache.

       'Dependencies.toml' is written only if the dependencies are resolved
       and compiled without errors, including imports of packages that cannot
       be resolved. Other errors in the package do not fail the command;
       'bal build' reports them.

       A package that already has a 'Dependencies.toml' is already
       initialized, so the command skips it and succeeds. 'bal build'
       keeps the dependencies of an initialized package up to date.


EXAMPLES
       Initialize the dependencies of the package in the current directory.
           $ bal init
